    "uncited": [
     "**Index Volume Population:** The index volume $I$ is populated to reflect the octree structure.",
     "When sampling the octree (for merging or debugging), the world position is mapped to an element in the index volume.",
     "The value in the index volume is used to do a second mapping into the correct octree level.",
     "The complication is that there are $l$ index volume elements that could be picked for each world space position.",
     "*   **Time Complexity:** Propagation is performed on each level individually.",
     "*   **History:** Builds on the original Light Propagation Volumes technique by Kaplanyan and Dachsbacher [KD10] and the concept of storing pre-computed indirect illumination using spherical harmonics by Sloan et al. [SKS02]."
    ]
   }
  }
